    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "$$2.43 - 1.2 = 1.23$$\nAlternatively, we can express 1.2 as a fraction, $1.2 = \\frac{6}{5}$. Then, we can have:\n\n$$\\frac{6}{5} - \\frac{10}{5} = \\frac{-4}{5}$$\nAnd multiplying the numerator and denominator by 2 to have a negative numerator:\n\n$$\\frac{-8}{10} = \\boxed{\\text{C}}$$\n\nWhat is the value of $\\arcsin 1$?\nThe function $\\arcsin x$, also known as the inverse sine function, returns the angle whose sine is $x$. In the context of this problem, we need to find the angle $\\theta$ such that $\\sin \\theta = 1$ and $\\theta$ lies within the range of the arcsine function, which is $\\left[-\\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right]$. \n\nThe sine of an angle in the range $\\left[-\\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right]$ that gives a value of 1 is $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$. \n\nThus, the value of $\\arcsin 1$ is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\).",
